Arguments:
  (none)

Description:
  This command lets you read and change your Unix .plan file.

  .plan is a traditional Unix file where a user can write a short
  presentation, current information, or anything else intended to be
  displayed through the finger service.

  SklaffKOM automatically creates your .plan file if it does not already
  exist. The file is edited using the standard SklaffKOM editor.

Note:
  .plan is completely separate from your SklaffKOM signature. The
  signature is changed with the "Change signature" command.

  The fact that SklaffKOM can create and edit .plan does not automatically
  mean that its contents can be read through finger from other computers.
  This depends on how the SysOp has configured the finger service and the
  system's file permissions.

  If you cancel the editor, no changes are saved.

